 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nDocument relationships not working correctly after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nI'm having issues with document relationships after updating to the latest version. When working with Word documents that contain relationships (like images, external links, etc.), the behavior seems to have changed and is causing problems.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\n# Try to open a document with images or external relationships\ndoc = Document('document_with_images.docx')\n\n# This used to work but now behaves unexpectedly\nfor part in doc.part.package.image_parts:\n    print(part.partname)\n\n# Also having issues when iterating through document content\nfor element in doc.iter_inner_content():\n    print(type(element))\n```\n\nThe relationships seem to be getting truncated or not properly identified as internal vs external. External relationships are being treated as internal and vice versa, and some relationship collections are returning incomplete results.\n\n#### Expected vs Actual Behavior\n\nExpected: External relationships should be properly identified and internal relationships should resolve to correct part names.\n\nActual: External relationships are being treated as internal, relationship collections are missing the last item, and target part names are not resolving correctly.\n</issue>\n",
